                "senderName": "NWS Pueblo CO",
                "headline": "Dust Storm Warning issued July 8 at 3:46PM MDT until July 8 at 4:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
                "description": "The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Dust Storm Warning for...\nAlamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\nWest central Huerfano County in southeastern Colorado...\nCostilla County in south central Colorado...\nSoutheastern Saguache County in central Colorado...\nEastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* Until 445 PM MDT.\n\n* At 344 PM MDT, widespread blowing dust due to thundertorm outflows\nwas over the eastern half of the San Luis Valley, with visibility\nnear Alamosa reported to be less than a quarter mile.\n\nHAZARD...Less than a quarter mile visibility with winds 50 to 60\nmph.\n\nSOURCE...Trained weather spotters.\n\nIMPACT...Dangerous life-threatening travel.\n\nLocations impacted include... Alamosa, San Luis Valley Airport,\nManassa, Sanford, La Jara, Antonito, San Luis, Romeo,\nBlanca, Crestone, Moffat, Hooper, Great Sand Dunes, San\nPablo, Alamosa East, Mesita, Fort Garland, Sanchez\nReservoir, San Luis Lake, and San Acacio.",
                "instruction": "Dust storms lead to dangerous driving conditions with visibility\nreduced to near zero. If driving, avoid dust storms if possible. If\ncaught in one, pull off the road, turn off your lights and keep your\nfoot off the brake.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "DSWPUB"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WOUS45 KPUB 082146"
                    ],
